{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor correctly escalated high-risk fetal status (RC1), assessed acute signals (RC2), set safe Clexane boundaries (RC3), avoided remote judgment with incomplete records (RC4), and gave executable day-of plan with teach-back and handoff (RC5/RC6). No serious RC error occurred and no minor RC error was identified; all six responsibility-chain items are met. High-order behaviors HO1, HO2, HO3, and HO4 were each actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact, making the trajectory Strong->Perfect. Since four case-defined high-order points exist, the maximum grade is 5, but achieving all four beyond-minimum items with distinct evidence satisfies at least two and therefore qualifies for 5.",
